  "details": "# Issue:\n\nRight now we have to make our own color themes to fit with the existing VRChat+ backgrounds. This can be a bit annoying / time consuming for users who just want their menu colors to fit with their background, especially as not everyone is really that good / willing to spend a lot of time at finding good color combinations.\n\n# Suggestion:\n\nGive each VRChat+ Background a fitting color theme.\n\n**I could see this being implemented the following way:**  \n\n- each background comes with it's own fitting theme  \n\n- in the UI Themes settings there would be an additional standard theme called \"Background\"\n\n- The colors of said Theme would always adjust depending on what background you have selected\n\n- The tooltip for said Theme could be \"Automatically selected fitting UI Colors for your selected Background\"\n\nDoing it this way would minimize UI clutter while still making it pretty easy to understand.",
